=== SURVEY ===
Web source TimeStamp.tsx is the shared timestamp renderer with a hover-tooltip alternate. It renders
ONE format in the visible <span> (relative "2h ago" or absolute "Apr 4, 2026, 2:30 AM") and ALWAYS
shows the OTHER format in a <Tooltip>, so power users can flip perspectives without leaving the page.
Props: value (string | number | Date | null | undefined), format ('relative' | 'absolute' | 'auto',
default 'auto'), in (TzMode), className. Logic:
  pref       = useTimeFormatPreference()            // 'relative' | 'absolute', default 'relative'
  {fmtDT, fmtRel} = useDateFormat(in)               // locale + IANA-tz aware
  if value == null → <span>—</span>                 // NO tooltip
  date = new Date(value); if isNaN → <span>—</span> // NO tooltip
  effective = format==='auto' ? pref : format
  primary   = effective==='relative' ? fmtRel(date) : fmtDT(date)
  secondary = effective==='relative' ? fmtDT(date) : fmtRel(date)   // the OTHER format
  → <Tooltip content={secondary}><span>{primary}</span></Tooltip>
The helpers (web/src/lib/dateFormat.ts): formatDateTime = "Apr 4, 2026, 2:30 AM"; formatRelative =
"just now" (<60s) / "{m}m ago" (<60m) / "{h}h ago" (<24h) / "{d}d ago" (<7d) / else formatDate
("Apr 4, 2026"). useDateFormat resolves locale (resolveLocale) + IANA zone (resolveTimezone over the
in-mode / vehicle zone / user override). The component extracts NO t() call (anonymous surface);
imports only @/components/ui Tooltip + the two hooks + TzMode.
Existing native: no TimeStamp* symbols (TimestampTool in feature-views is unrelated; case-distinct).
No collision. Canonical predecessor studied: shared-surfaces/DateTime (0084) — the sibling
date/time renderer the web TimeStamp explicitly mirrors ("Mirrors the in prop on <DateTime>"); repo
convention is per-surface self-contained types (DateTime re-implements resolveLocale/resolveTimezone
rather than importing the web lib), which this surface follows (own TimeStampTzMode etc.).

=== REASONING ===
- The web component is a near-pure renderer that voices two formats (visible + tooltip alternate);
  the prompt requires a production-polished native surface reproducing its DATA, composition, states,
  and (native-chrome) i18n, every state visible (no blank box). Chosen architecture mirrors the
  canonical DateTime(0084) leaf, per-surface self-contained types:
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): TimeStampResolve seam; TimeStampFormat (relative/absolute/auto);
    TimeStampPreference (relative/absolute); TimeStampTzMode (web TzMode); TimeStampValue
    (date/iso/epochMillis/absent — the web string|number|Date|null union, epoch read as MILLISECONDS
    like new Date(number)); TimeStampFormatContext; TimeStampFormatting (parse + resolveLocale +
    resolveTimezone + effective + pair + the verbatim formatRelative/formatDateTime/formatDate ports +
    {{count}} interpolation); TimeStampPair (primary+secondary); TimeStampAccessibility (value label +
    alternate hint).
  • Model: TimeStampTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default; TimeStampConnection axis;
    TimeStampInput snapshot (value + format + mode + preference + locale/zone context + lifecycle);
    @Observable TimeStampModel (binds the source, view.opened once, one-shot stale auto-refresh);
    TimeStampStrings i18n facade (table "TimeStamp").
  • Projection: TimeStampResolved (phase + primary + secondary + a11y) + TimeStampProjection.resolve
    (error → loading → null/invalid "—" empty → content w/ primary+secondary pair).
  • Seams: TimeStampSource protocol, LiveTimeStampSource (host value/context bridge), InMemory source.
  • States: loading skeleton, error (TSQueryError peer). Views: value label (primary body + secondary
    as the hover tooltip via .help (web Tooltip→macOS pointer help) + VoiceOver hint), freshness chip.
  • TimeStamp.swift (surfaceSlug "TimeStamp", phase switch, freshness chip, onAppear/onDisappear) +
    Previews + strings + Tests + ModelTests.
- States rendered: loading (skeleton line), empty (the muted "—" fallback inline, never blank — web
  behavior + P4 leaf contract), error (retry — web QueryError peer), content (visible body + tooltip
  alternate), plus the orthogonal connection axis stale/offline (freshness chip + one-shot
  auto-refresh on the stale transition; last value stays visible).
- Rejected: porting Tailwind/className (native uses P1/S9 tokens); reusing DateTime's TimeZoneMode
  symbol (kept per-surface self-contained so the surface type-checks + unit-tests in isolation);
  inventing a tap/long-press flip interaction (web is a passive label with a hover tooltip — kept
  parity via .help + a11y hint, the DateTime precedent); an ISO-title tooltip (that is DateTime's
  behavior; TimeStamp's tooltip is the ALTERNATE FORMAT, not the ISO); HTTP in the view (bound via
  the source seam); formatRelativeTime (DateTime's variant — TimeStamp uses formatRelative, which has
  lowercase "just now", a {d}d-ago bucket, and a date-only >7d fallback).

